menu "sys_system"

    config SYS_SYSTEM_DEADMAN_DEFAULT_MS
        int "Dead-man timeout at boot (ms, 0 = off)"
        default 0
        range 0 60000
        help
          0, or the master's and the clients' sessions' timeout (150..60000):
          their end enters the safe state. Changed at runtime with the sys
          DEADMAN command; not stored.

    config SYS_SYSTEM_TIME_PERIOD_S
        int "Time broadcast period (s)"
        default 60
        range 5 3600
        help
          The root sends its time to every board this often (and when a client
          sets it, and when a board is reached), so the clocks of all boards
          are the root's.

endmenu
